  "invariants": [
    "The provider constructs the original NSSearchField/NSSearchFieldCell. Existing native field editors, text models, clipboard, filters, focus, native key interpretation and drawing are shared.",
    "The search-part query consumes the actual native cell button/text rectangles; no icon, layout, hit inset, clear algorithm or control implementation is copied.",
    "The cancel observer snapshots native pre-action text/selection, forwards the original native button target/action and proposes its actual clear result through the existing edit filter. Ordinary text-change actions do not enter this scope.",
    "Chromium PaintSearchField delegates to the existing guarded PaintTextField boundary. Its hidden shadow widget click default is suppressed for trusted owned search clicks while page listeners remain active.",
    "Native delete: uses DeleteBackward so the existing guarded deletion hook installs its native proposed range after beforeinput. No new engine call or copied editing algorithm is added.",
    "Both pointer release bindings validate control identity after callbacks; Firefox consumes a retired gesture before invoking the original stale widget post handler.",
    "API 1 retains the existing 584-byte prefix and all earlier kind numbers. New loader/old provider behavior is explicitly tested: no search capability/control, empty new part query, and existing fields still construct.",
    "Browser address bars, toolbars and tabs remain original. Search submit/activation, recents, placeholders, broader native key/IME/accessibility behavior and the overall browser-then-GTK/Qt/KDE goal remain open."
  ]
